---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Bridge from "../../components/Bridge.astro";
---

<BaseLayout lang="en" title="EM-I-CLEAR" description="An independent nonprofit closing the gap the system leaves between people who suddenly need care and the people who can give it — through education, research, and responsible technology.">
  <section class="story-hero story-hero--home">
    <div class="container story-hero__content">
      <p class="hero-label">Independent nonprofit · Republic of Korea</p>
      <h1>For a world where<br />no one has to suffer.</h1>
      <p class="story-hero__lead">We close the gap the system leaves between people who suddenly need care and the people who can give it.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button-solid" href="#story">What we do</a>
        <a class="button button-ghost" href="/en/projects/">Education &amp; Research</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <a class="scroll-cue" href="#opening"><span>Scroll</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
  </section>

  <section id="opening" class="opening-statement">
    <div class="container opening-statement__inner" data-reveal>
      <p class="section-label">The problem we see</p>
      <h2>It is not the people.<br />It is the system.</h2>
      <p>Inside the hospital, the gaps no single doctor can fill keep piling up. From outside, none of that is visible. Where the system that should connect people has stopped working, a gap has opened.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="approach" class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading" data-reveal>
        <p class="section-label">Our approach</p>
        <h2>One step,<br />from each side.</h2>
        <p>Between someone who suddenly falls ill and the people who could help, there is a gap the system never filled. We close it from both sides.</p>
      </div>
      <Bridge lang="en" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="story" class="story-sequence" aria-label="What EM-I-CLEAR does">
    <article id="programs" class="story-chapter container">
      <figure class="story-media story-media--phone" data-reveal>
        <span class="story-media__index" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <img src="/images/smartphone-unsplash-1678522345215.jpg" alt="A hand looking at a smartphone" width="2400" height="1600" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Being able to describe what is wrong.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="story-copy" data-reveal>
        <p class="chapter-label">Technology · Toward the provider</p>
        <h3>Technology<br />closes the gap.</h3>
        <p>We help people take stock of their own condition and put it into the language of medicine, and work out with them whether this is a moment that needs a clinician.</p>
        <a class="arrow-link" href="/en/projects/#technology">Emergency decision support <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="story-chapter story-chapter--reverse container">
      <figure class="story-media story-media--portrait" data-reveal>
        <span class="story-media__index" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <img src="/images/empty-classroom-pexels-30105084.jpg" alt="An empty learning space filled with sunlight" width="2200" height="2933" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>More people who can carry the load.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="story-copy" data-reveal>
        <p class="chapter-label">Education · Toward the patient</p>
        <h3>We train the people<br />who provide care.</h3>
        <p>Residents and medical students work through emergencies again and again, then look back together at the decisions they made and at how the team communicated.</p>
        <a class="arrow-link" href="/en/projects/#education">Simulation education <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="story-chapter container">
      <figure class="story-media" data-reveal>
        <span class="story-media__index" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <img src="/images/pediatric-tools-pexels-4491759.jpg" alt="Toy medical tools used for child-friendly health education" width="2000" height="3000" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Starting where the gap is widest.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="story-copy" data-reveal>
        <p class="chapter-label">Priority · Children &amp; adolescents</p>
        <h3>We start<br />here.</h3>
        <p>When no hospital can accept a patient, children and adolescents are turned away first. This is where the gap has opened widest.</p>
        <a class="arrow-link" href="/en/about/">The problem we see <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="nonprofit-panel nonprofit-panel--minimal">
    <div class="container nonprofit-panel__inner" data-reveal>
      <p class="nonprofit-panel__minimal-label">Independent nonprofit</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
